   "question": "הפונקציה $f:\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}\\to A$ מוגדרת לפי הכלל $f(k)=k^2\\pmod6+\\operatorname{lcm}(2,\\gcd(2,k))$ לכל $k\\in\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}$.\nמצאו את $A$ כך ש-$f$ היא פונקציה על.",
   "solution": "חישוב הערכים:\n```\nf(1) = 1 (mod 6) + lcm(2, gcd(2,1)) = 1 + lcm(2,1) = 1 + 2 = 3\nf(2) = 4 (mod 6) + lcm(2, gcd(2,2)) = 4 + lcm(2,2) = 4 + 2 = 6\nf(3) = 9 (mod 6) + lcm(2, gcd(2,3)) = 3 + lcm(2,1) = 3 + 2 = 5\nf(4) = 16 (mod 6) + lcm(2, gcd(2,4)) = 4 + lcm(2,2) = 4 + 2 = 6\nf(5) = 25 (mod 6) + lcm(2, gcd(2,5)) = 1 + lcm(2,1) = 1 + 2 = 3\nf(6) = 36 (mod 6) + lcm(2, gcd(2,6)) = 0 + lcm(2,2) = 2\n```\n$A=f(\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\})=\\{2,3,5,6\\}\\iff f$ על, כי לכל $y\\in A$ קיים מקור.",
   "solutionSource": "student-solution",
