   "question": "הוכיחו באינדוקציה שלכל $1\\le n\\in\\mathbb{N}$ מתקיים:\n$$\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5}+\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 9}+\\frac{1}{9\\cdot 13}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{(4n-3)\\cdot(4n+1)}=\\frac{n}{4n+1}$$",
   "solution": "**I. בסיס:** $P(1)$: $\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5}=\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 1+1}\\Rightarrow P(1)=\\text{TRUE}$.\n**II. צעד:** $P(k)=T$ עבור $1\\le k\\in\\mathbb{N}$ $\\Rightarrow$ $P(k+1)=T$.\n$P(k):\\ \\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5}+\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 9}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{(4k-3)(4k+1)}=\\frac{k}{4k+1}$\n$P(k+1):\\ \\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{(4k+1)(4k+5)}=\\frac{k+1}{4k+5}$\n$$\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{(4k-3)(4k+1)}+\\frac{1}{(4k+1)(4k+5)}=\\frac{k}{4k+1}+\\frac{1}{(4k+1)(4k+5)}=\\frac{4k^2+5k+1}{(4k+1)(4k+5)}=\\frac{(4k^2+4k)+(k+1)}{(4k+1)(4k+5)}$$\n$$=\\frac{4k(k+1)+(k+1)}{(4k+1)(4k+5)}=\\frac{(4k+1)(k+1)}{(4k+1)(4k+5)}=\\frac{k+1}{4k+5}\\Rightarrow P(k+1)=TRUE$$\nמסקנה: מ-I ו-II לכל $1\\le n\\in\\mathbb{N}$ מתקיים $P(n)=TRUE$.",
   "solutionSource": "lecturer-solution",
   "official": true,
   "confidence": "high",
